{"id": 56, "ts": 1780142203.3466465, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I appreciate the additional insight on Candidate\u202fD, especially the clear strengths in problem\u2011solving, concentration and a serious sense of responsibility. However, the concerns about a hot temper and a \u201cknow\u2011it\u2011all\u201d attitude directly undermine crew cooperation and professional communication\u2014areas that are non\u2011negotiable for long\u2011distance operations.\nCandidate\u202fB, on the other hand, is described as very conscientious (a strong indicator of operational reliability) and handles stress very well, which addresses both reliability and stress\u2011resilience criteria. While B can be grumpy and occasionally uncooperative, those traits are less severe than D\u2019s documented arrogance and hot\u2011tempered behavior, and B\u2019s proven stress handling gives us confidence he will maintain composure under pressure.\nGiven the balance of evidence, I continue to recommend **Candidate\u202fB** for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
